<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Dec 31.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - Dec 31.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on December 30. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name		   P/E	 Close</p>
<p>1   Tourism Asset	 3566.67    1.07</p>
<p>2   Portman Min	    373.02    2.35</p>
<p>3   Niugini Min	    223.02    3.10</p>
<p>4   Mayne Nickless	 189.18    8.57</p>
<p>5   Adel Bton Cement     124.64    1.72</p>
<p>6   Colonial Coml	  122.95    2.25</p>
<p>7   Forrestania Gold	87.81    2.45</p>
<p>8   Westral Forest	  85.14    2.35</p>
<p>9   Countrywide-PP	  83.94    1.15</p>
<p>10  Herald Rsc		79.65    0.90</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p>1   Dominion Min	     2.16    0.94</p>
<p>2   Consol Rutile	    3.19    0.90</p>
<p>3   Computer Power	   3.74    3.83</p>
<p>4   Premier Inv		4.51    0.80</p>
<p>5   Queensland Cotton	5.67    4.30</p>
<p>6   Parbury Ltd		6.08    0.72</p>
<p>7   BTR Plc		    6.45    6.00</p>
<p>8   OLS Asia Hldgs	   7.39    0.88</p>
<p>9   Aust Gold Rsc	    7.45    1.36</p>
<p>10  Templeton Global	 7.71    1.35</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
